From 699ae91b17b381cf579f83709c1d33103cba204d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:32:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AdaptiveStream] Fix seeks at segment and chapter boundaries
 and at a quality change

Requires the TS patch.

- Fix a seek to the time of a key frame, which continued at the next key
  frame: the seek time in milliseconds came with a float error
- Fix a seek to an earlier time inside the current segment, which
  continued at the start of the segment instead of at the frame of the
  seek time
- Fix the period ends of a live DASH stream with more than one period
  and a SegmentList, or a SegmentTimeline with a presentationTimeOffset,
  which waited for segments after a complete period, or continued at the
  next period before the period was complete
- Fix a forward seek in a TS video stream, which continued at the next
  segment instead of at the next key frame, and ended the playback in
  the last segment
- Fix a seek to the start time of some segments, which chose the segment
  before: a TS seek downloaded and scanned one more segment, and a seek
  to the frame at or before the seek time continued in the segment
  before
- Fix a change of the stream quality in a TS stream, which lost the last
  frames of the old quality: two video frames, and the audio frames that
  waited for a PTS
- Fix a seek to the start time of some chapters, and to the start time
  of a segment between two microseconds (for example at a 90 kHz
  timescale), which continued in the chapter or segment before
- Fix a change of the stream quality that could start before the reader
  of the old quality returned all frames, while a read of the next frame
  was still in progress
- Fix a seek during a change of the stream quality: a seek into the
  segment of the change read data of the new quality into the reader of
  the old quality, and a seek to the first segment continued at the
  segment of the change
- Fix a possible crash at a change of the stream quality: the reopen of
  the stream allocated more segment buffers while a download used the
  buffers
- Fix a seek during a change of the stream quality, which continued at
  the start of the segment instead of at the seek time
- Fix wrong stream times, a wrong seek limit of a live stream and seeks
  to the wrong segment with a high timescale or large times (for example
  times from 1970 at 90 kHz), where a time conversion overflowed
- Fix a DASH SegmentList without a timescale, whose segment times
  counted in microseconds instead of seconds
- Fix a possible crash at a seek after the playback stopped for a
  missing decrypter
- Fix a chapter selection after a failed seek, which returned to the
  time of the failed seek

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
